      'so the Renaissance looked BACKWARD to recover the wisdom and beauty of antiquity and expressed itself mainly through art and letters the Enlightenment looked FORWARD building new systems of government and knowledge and expressed itself mainly through philosophy political theory and natural science the Scientific Revolution roughly 1543 to 1687 Copernicus Galileo Newton bridges the two',
