      'the BOLSHEVIKS led by LENIN wanted a small tightly disciplined centralised VANGUARD party of professional revolutionaries and believed Russia could move rapidly to a proletarian socialist revolution even though it was still largely peasant and semi feudal skipping a long capitalist phase they seized power in the October Revolution of 1917 and became the Communist Party',
      'the MENSHEVIKS led by MARTOV wanted a broad open MASS party like Western European social democratic parties and held to a more orthodox Marxist view that Russia must first pass through a BOURGEOIS DEMOCRATIC capitalist stage before socialism was possible so they favoured cooperating with liberals and a gradual approach they were NOT capitalists they were Marxist socialists just more moderate and gradualist the Bolsheviks crushed them after 1917',
