      'the CENTRAL POWERS were GERMANY and AUSTRIA HUNGARY the core of the old Triple Alliance joined by the OTTOMAN EMPIRE in 1914 and BULGARIA in 1915 they are called Central because they sat in the centre of Europe geographically surrounded by the Entente to the west east and south which is why Germany faced the strategic problem of a two front war',
